# Copy to .env.development.local (gitignored) and fill in your DEV project.
#
# `npm run dev` reads .env.development.local; `npm run build` reads the
# committed .env.production. Neither falls back to the other — leave these
# blank and the app stops on a "not configured" screen rather than quietly
# opening the real logbook.
#
# Setting up the dev project, once:
#   1. supabase.com → New project (free tier is enough), any name.
#   2. SQL editor → run migrations/001…005 in order, one at a time.
#   3. Settings → API → copy "Project URL" and the "anon public" key here.
#   4. Authentication → sign yourself up; it is a separate account from prod.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
